<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masalit people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Masalit are a people of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a>, speaking a language of the Maban family and living mainly as farmers. In the late 19th century they formed the sultanate of Dar Masalit, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-geneina">El Geneina</a>, which resisted both Darfur and the French before passing under British rule in Sudan in the 1920s. They suffered heavily in the Darfur conflicts after 2003.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masalit-people.jpg" alt="Masalit people" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ermanarich · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Masalit.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
